  "text": " So you just kind of parenthetically noted that this was a, as you put it, a violation of medical ethics. For those of us who aren't medical ethicists, how specifically would these mandates violate medical ethics? Well, the central principle of medical ethics, and whether this is research ethics or clinical ethics at the bedside, is the principle of informed consent. And this was first articulated in some legal codes, but very, very publicly, following World War II in the Nuremberg Code, which many people have heard of. Most people haven't read, and I encourage viewers to go read the Nuremberg Code. I have read it. It's like 10 sentences long. Yes. It's less than a page. And the basic principle in the Nuremberg Code is the principle of free and informed consent.",
